 "notebook": {
  "title": "WAVE DANCER PROTOTYPE",
  "subtitle": "",
  "text": "# What's going on?\nCurrently there's a transition from the 'State' window that's running $2p_{-1}$, $2p_{1}$, $4p_{-1}$, and $4d_{2}$ in STATE-A and $2s_{0}$, $2p_{0}$, $4p_{1}$, and $4d_{-2}$ in STATE-B. The level 2 and 4 shells make for some interesting geometries tri-bubbles from the center. STATE-A and B's level 4 orbitals\n\nNot to be confused with actual hybridized orbitals btw.\n\n# Styling\nBest in Dark Mode imo. This is a good time to test out palettes and see what kind of designs ya'll can do. I think the demo goes for 'signed' by default but I've set an inverse automation for 'exposure' and 'soft' so that if you want to switch to 'ADD' or 'CLOUD' styles, they go along with da beat.\n\nIf you're not into the flickering background, it can be disabled removing the macro in Settings > Display > Stage and then remove the macro by click and holding the knob's label. It looks sick with the 'ADD' wave style though.\n\n_- Josh_\n"
 }
}